			<item>
				<title>GoTo Conferences!!!1!</title>
				<link>https://www.andreffs.com/blog/goto-conferences/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 13 Jun 2024 17:29:18 +0100</pubDate><author>andreffs18@gmail.com (André Silva)</author>
				<guid>https://www.andreffs.com/blog/goto-conferences/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;I really enjoy conferences. I think it&amp;rsquo;s one of the best things the tech industry has!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Covid stopped us from going to &amp;ldquo;in-person&amp;rdquo; conferences, and we all had to shift to a more &amp;ldquo;remote&amp;rdquo; or &amp;ldquo;online&amp;rdquo; version of it. You still got to see some great talks, but there&amp;rsquo;s a world of difference between how you experience and learn from them.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This year I&amp;rsquo;ve finally got back to an &amp;ldquo;in-person&amp;rdquo; conference, and being so excited about attending one again I started making a list of what I should do to make the most out of it.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Tools vs Data Structures</title>
				<link>https://www.andreffs.com/blog/tools-vs-data-structures/</link>
				<pubDate>Thu, 16 Feb 2023 07:27:00 +0000</pubDate><author>andreffs18@gmail.com (André Silva)</author>
				<guid>https://www.andreffs.com/blog/tools-vs-data-structures/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Usually, when interviewing for an engineering or software position, you end up doing some sort of &amp;ldquo;coding challenge&amp;rdquo;. A friend of mine has recently left the company and is doing one at the moment. He asked me for help on solving a particular challenge, which I felt was a good exercise for me.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This blog post talks a bit about the challenge and my approach to solving it. Also, this post works as a personal reminder that sometimes it is not about picking the best tool, but the right data structure.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>n8n customizations for Production</title>
				<link>https://www.andreffs.com/blog/n8n-customizations-for-production/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 17 May 2021 16:58:27 +0100</pubDate><author>andreffs18@gmail.com (André Silva)</author>
				<guid>https://www.andreffs.com/blog/n8n-customizations-for-production/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This post is a continuation on &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.andreffs.com/blog/setup-n8n-on-kubernetes&#34;&gt;&amp;ldquo;Setup n8n on Kubernetes&amp;rdquo;&lt;/a&gt;, so most of the things we talk here assume that you&amp;rsquo;ve followed/read this one as well.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;hr&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;After running n8n during a couple of months in production, me and my team realized that the default configuration do not work very well for us.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;So here in this post I go over the changes we did to allow n8n to scale and work without problems.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
