				<description>&lt;p&gt;Since this &lt;em&gt;#remotelife&lt;/em&gt; began, sadly not for the best reasons, I&amp;rsquo;ve been able to finally clean my backlog of, guess what, TV Shows, Games, Podcasts, Books&amp;hellip; Well, everything that a person is suppose to do!&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Very happy was I until I remembered that, maybe I should start looking into the &lt;strong&gt;&amp;ldquo;To Read&amp;rdquo;&lt;/strong&gt; bookmarks, &lt;strong&gt;&amp;ldquo;Saved&amp;rdquo;&lt;/strong&gt; on Reddit and, the holy grail, &lt;strong&gt;&amp;ldquo;Read Later&amp;rdquo;&lt;/strong&gt; of Feedly.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;bookmarks.png&#34; alt=&#34;All bookmarks&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;While the &amp;ldquo;Saved&amp;rdquo; section on Reddit was mostly threads from &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.reddit.com/r/cscareerquestions/&#34;&gt;/r/cscarrearquestions&lt;/a&gt; (and some memes from &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.reddit.com/r/wallstreetbets&#34;&gt;/r/wsb&lt;/a&gt; 😂) the other two places were actual interesting articles that I have planned on reading.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
